  "id": "DrugBank_DB14568 - MONDO_15667",
  "verbalization": "Ivosidenib is associated with Unclassified Acute Myeloid Leukemia through a chain of indications involving Mitoxantrone. The drug is linked to Acute Myeloblastic Leukemia Without Maturation and Acute Myeloid Leukemia And Myelodysplastic Syndromes Related To Topoisomerase Type 2 Inhibitor, all of which are indicated to interact with Mitoxantrone. Since Mitoxantrone is a known inducer of Unclassified Acute Myeloid Leukemia, the indirect pathway through these indications suggests a potential role for Ivosidenib in the development or progression of this leukemia subtype. The evidence is consistent across multiple paths, reinforcing the hypothesis that Ivosidenib may contribute to the pathogenesis of Unclassified Acute Myeloid Leukemia via its interaction with Mitoxantrone. The mechanism appears to rely on the shared biological pathway involving topoisomerase inhibitors and their downstream effects on leukemia progression.",
